## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of end-to-end testing in a complex, multi-region, event-sourced delivery application. It checks whether the candidate can design tests that cover data isolation, cross-region convergence, failure handling, and compliance scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- Event-sourced E2E flows with Kafka domain topics and region-specific read models
- Cross-region consistency and latency budget validation
- Multi-tenant data isolation and DSAR (Data Subject Access Request) compliance
- Fault injection including regional outages and retry mechanisms
- Observability integration and deterministic seed data

## Code Example
```javascript
// Seed deterministic test data and publish events to Kafka; verify read-model convergence
const seedOrder = { id: 'ORD-123', tenantId: 'tenant-acme', region: 'us-east' };

await kafka.publish('orders.us-east', { 
  eventType: 'OrderPlaced', 
  payload: seedOrder, 
  timestamp: '2026-01-15T10:00:00Z' 
});

await kafka.publish('drivers.us-east', {
  eventType: 'DriverAssigned',
  payload: { orderId: 'ORD-123', driverId: 'DRV-456' }
});

// Verify real-time WebSocket delivery to clients
const wsUpdate = await waitForWebSocketMessage('rider-client', 'ETAUpdated');
expect(wsUpdate.payload.eta).toBeWithinSLA();

// Validate cross-region read-model convergence
const readModel = await readModelClient.query('us-west', 'orders', { id: 'ORD-123' });
expect(readModel.status).toEqual('confirmed');
expect(readModel.convergenceTime).toBeLessThan(SLA_THRESHOLD_MS);

// Verify tenant isolation
const crossTenantResult = await readModelClient.query('us-east', 'orders', { 
  id: 'ORD-123', 
  tenantId: 'tenant-foreign' 
});
expect(crossTenantResult.accessDenied).toBe(true);

// DSAR deletion verification
await dsarService.requestDeletion('customer-789');
await waitForEventProcessing();
const piiCheck = await readModelClient.scanAllRegions('customer-789');
expect(piiCheck.found).toBe(false);

// Region failover test
await regionOutageSimulator.failover('us-east', 'us-west');
const failoverState = await readModelClient.getState('us-west', 'ORD-123');
expect(failoverState.reconstructed).toBe(true);
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests in privacy-preserving analytics must guarantee erasure across all data stores, including caches, materialized views, and backups, while maintaining accurate audit trails for compliance.

## Key Concepts
- DSAR data erasure across microservices
- Event sourcing and tombstone propagation
- Soft vs hard deletes and retention windows
- Cross-region replication and data consistency
- Audit logs and backups scrub policy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test outline for DSAR flow
test('DSAR end-to-end erasure', async () => {
  seedTestUser();
  ingestEvents();
  triggerDSAR();
  await expect(dataRemovedFromPrimaryDB()).toBe(true);
  await expect(eventStoreHasDeletion()).toBe(true);
  await expect(cacheInvalidated()).toBe(true);
  await expect(auditLogsContain('DSAR')).toBe(true);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate that backups are scrubbed after the retention window without impacting restore capabilities?
- What observability signals would you add to detect DSAR failures in a multi-region deployment?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a complex, cross-origin integration scenario with iframe messaging, localStorage persistence, and multi-tenant isolation—common in partner ecosystems like Salesforce, Cloudflare, and Coinbase. It probes reliability under network blips and ensures data integrity across domains.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-origin messaging via postMessage between host and iframe
- Frame targeting with frameLocator/selectors
- Draft persistence in localStorage and autosave recovery
- Network fault injection and retry semantics
- Tenant data isolation across partner domains

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright sketch (conceptual only)
const host = page.locator('#host-app');
const frame = host.frameLocator('iframe#widget-form');
await frame.locator('input[name="name"]').fill('Acme Corp');
// simulate cross-origin event
await page.evaluate(() => {
  window.postMessage({type: 'INIT', tenant: 'tenantA'}, '*');
});
// flaky submit
await page.route('https://api.partner.com/submit', route => {
  route.fulfill({ status: 500, body: '{}' });
